     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Deep branch / posterior interosseous nerve:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " the deep branch supplies extensor carpi radialis brevis and supinator, then continues as the posterior interosseous nerve to extensor digitorum, extensor digiti minimi, extensor carpi ulnaris, extensor indicis, extensor pollicis longus and brevis, and abductor pollicis longus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
