    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Carpal tunnel signs:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " radial-palmar hand paresthesias and wrist and palm pain (may radiate to the forearm and shoulder, may be worse at night); later sensory loss over the palmar first 3 fingers and weak, atrophied thumb abduction and opposition."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Carpal tunnel risk factors:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " pregnancy, diabetes, hypothyroidism, some forms of amyloidosis, rheumatoid arthritis and repeated forceful work with the wrist extended; most cases are idiopathic."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
